\section*{The four-dimensional normalized-volume gap}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
The normalized volume of a singular complex klt fourfold germ with zero boundary is claimed to be at most $162$, attained precisely by ordinary double points. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} For a singular boundary-zero klt closed point $x$ of a normal complex algebraic fourfold with rational Cartier $K_X$, OpenAI claims
\[
\widehat{\operatorname{vol}}(x,X)\le162,
\qquad\text{equality}\ \Longleftrightarrow\ (X,x)_{\mathrm{an}}\simeq(\{z_0^2+\cdots+z_4^2=0\}\subset\mathbb C^5,0).
\]
Normalized volume is the infimum of $A_X(v)^4\operatorname{vol}(v)$ over valuations centered at $x$, with $\operatorname{vol}(v)$ the asymptotic valuation-ideal colength multiplied by $4!$. The theorem has zero boundary and complex dimension four.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 037, 2026-09-24): Density and integral discrepancy estimates reduce the high-volume cone to a terminal Gorenstein hyperplane section. Threefold classification bounds its embedding dimension, making the original cone a hypersurface; the established complete-intersection gap then gives the sharp bound and equality description.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
